findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests check file-not-found fallback but don't distinguish NotFound
    from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented sanitized Display on ServerError: ''server error: please
    try again later'' regardless of internal string. Reviewer verified: ''ServerError
    Display shows "server error: please try again later" regardless of the internal
    string. The internal detail is preserved only in Debug.'' Security test at security.rs:9-16
    confirms. However, the broader CliError Display with Io(#[error(transparent)])
    forwarding OS details to stderr was not flagged.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection prevention tests and Dev implemented CRLF rejection,
    but SiemClient.tenant_id remains a raw String rather than using TenantId from
    axiathon-core. The type-safety aspect (using validated TenantId instead of String)
    was not caught by any phase.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #4: ''RawConfig silently accepts unknown fields... A
    typo like servr_url will be silently ignored... there is no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]
    to catch typos.'' Explicitly mentions the token field being silently ignored as
    a usability trap.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ... always true). TEA wrote the test but the assertion logic itself is flawed
    and no phase caught it.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic via
    'let _ = config;' without assert_eq! on default values.
